      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Specialized Two-Wheeler &amp; Motorcycle Carrier Logistics &amp; Safety Engineering for Bike Transportation In Kalyandurg</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>In Kalyandurg, a hub for regional logistics, bike transportation has evolved into a highly engineered process that safeguards two‑wheelers during intercity movement. The core of this system is the specialized enclosed hydraulic ramp carrier, a self‑propelled unit that lifts a motorcycle onto a flat deck while the hydraulic rails lock the bike in place.</p>
<p>This design eliminates the need for manual lifting and reduces the risk of damage to the frame or suspension.</p>

<p>On the deck, each wheel is secured with an individual steel wheel‑lock chock. These chocks are engineered to clamp the tire against the deck surface with a force of 1,200 N, preventing any lateral shift.</p>
<p>The chocks are complemented by high‑tensile ratchet lashing that runs through a series of 3‑way locking points. The lashing is rated at 5,000 kg and is tensioned to 2,500 kg before the vehicle departs, ensuring the bike remains immobile even during high‑speed highway transit.</p>

